# the webassembly family: the targets whose values live in the locals of a
# function, whose control is structured, whose addresses are physical and
# which evaluate on an operand stack
#
# its build is masc's wasm set with the target's baseline and the extensions
# a build adds, its one convention row the basic c abi resolved with no
# register file, and its back end mirl.target.wasm.module, which makes one
# relocatable wasm object, of which mink's link makes the final module where
# the build's options ask for it. its rows are the register family's, in
# their order, after the markers of where a slot's storage begins and ends
# are erased, as no two slots share storage here, and the thread-local
# variables a target with one thread reaches as ordinary ones are made so: aggregate values taken apart, vectors
# split to what the build holds, binary16 computed in binary32, helpers, the
# abi's pieces, the aggregates and vectors they place taken apart, the
# reinterpretations through binary16 they make taken out, and the
# binary16 values passed by reference made encodings, the float stand ins, narrow arithmetic widened and wide integers split, the
# neutral optimisations of legal ir with dead code removal, the multiply forms
# and shift bounding, and the structurizer last, so the region tree the emitter reads is the
# graph as it is.

